{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>If you will deal falsely with me and with my offspring and with my descendants.</b> Avimelekh sought two covenants: the first, that Abraham would not drive his sons from their land; and the second, that they would not destroy for themselves the fruits of the land — this is what he said: ״ועם הארץ אשר גרתה בה״. And Abraham acknowledged the matter and said: ״אנכי אשבע״. And understand well that this oath is the first mentioned in the Torah, and because the word שבועה is derived from שבעה as is known in the Kabbalah, therefore Abraham set seven ewes of the flock, and called the place by the name of the oath: באר שבע; and likewise with Isaac we find that he called the well by the name of the oath." "And the matter is that one who swears is included in the seven called צרור החיים, and believes in the Torah and in the life of the world to come; and one who transgresses an oath denies the principle and removes himself from the category of the oath, and has no portion in the world to come." "And you already know that six upper extremities are His name, and six lower extremities are sealed in His name, and therefore the tradition came to the masters of truth concerning the utterance לא תשא, that the entire world trembled — which they did not say concerning the rest of the commandments." "<b>And understand</b> the secret of the language: you will not find from it a simple verb (קל) that says שבעו or שבע, but only נשבעו and נשבע — for the meaning of נשבע is: he brought himself into the category of the seven, if he fulfills his oath. And if he transgresses his oath, the meaning of נשבע will be: he removed himself from the category of the seven. So it is a word that includes a thing and its opposite, like ״ודשנו את המזבח״. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:05.263397479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}